      "message": "Hi David,\n\nIn order to make Citadel RPC call as simple as possible, I try to create two RPC call to handle SHA256 HASH init, update and CBOR encoding from Citadel side.\n\nvoid eicCborAppend(EicCbor* cbor, const uint8_t* data, size_t size) {\n    for (size_t n \u003d 0; n \u003c size; n++) {\n        cbor-\u003edata[cbor-\u003esize] \u003d data[n];\n        cbor-\u003esize +\u003d 1;\n        if (cbor-\u003esize \u003e\u003d EIC_MAX_CBOR_SIZE) {\n            cbor-\u003eops-\u003esha256Update(cbor-\u003edigester, cbor-\u003edata, cbor-\u003esize);\n+            cbor-\u003ecitadel_identity_rpc-\u003eWICcborSha256(HASH_UPDATE, cbor-\u003edata, cbor-\u003esize, NULL);\n            cbor-\u003esize \u003d 0;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCorresponding Citadel RPC call:\n\nhttps://nugget-os-review.googlesource.com/c/core/nugget/+/29925/1/user/identity/identity_support.c#782\n\n\nThank you,\nJoseph.",
